Z||000003||DXR_DAD||07-31-2000||11:53 PM||||Take a look here:<BR>I hope it helps. You can also use the search<BR>there are many post on this topic. Use the word (Glue) for the search word. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003114.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003114.html</A> <P>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=21451559&Sequence=2">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=99075&a=723595&p=16992154">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=21451561&Sequence=2">  <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723601&p=18231071&Sequence=1"> <P>Just a few pics of my first re-glue/repair and the carbon fiber by Rally. I'm now doing a color change and will go with real carbon fiber dash face plates!<P>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 08-01-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000004||tgowens||08-01-2000||12:02 AM||||here is the glue I used...... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/glue.jpg"> .......get several clamps from the hardware store and several paint stir sticks from the paint store -- glue the front side of the piece first, flatten with stir sticks on each side of the piece and clamp in place (this glue wil dry in 5 - 10 minutes) - then glue the edge the same way and finally the back side.......you'll never know the sun had warped or loosened the vinyl at all -- here is an example after I did mine...... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/my_interior_2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||08-01-2000||01:46 AM||||Gorilla Glue.||||reg||1
Z||000006||86SE||08-01-2000||02:57 AM||||Duct Tape..<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||08-01-2000||09:43 AM||||dare i say it...<P>i think so...<P><B>snot & thumb tacks</B> work best!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>jk<P>I tried the hot glue thing 10 years ago, didnt last!<P>i will be fixing mine this fall, DXR_DAD sent  me the Loctite stuff.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||08-01-2000||10:36 AM||||I was serious about the Gorilla Glue.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Master_Sushi||08-01-2000||12:55 PM||||I had the same problum a while ago with my fiero. I jsut took the pieces off with the problum and used a gel super glue. I put the super glue on and held it for about 30 secs... worked GREAT for me, looks new.<P>but im sure its one of those things where many ways will work just fine.||||reg||1
